<!bhtml 1>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>home.biggle</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="icon.png">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <script src="home.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a class="nav-home" href="./" aria-label="home.biggle"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
    <div class="nav-links">
      <a href="#sites">Sites</a>
      <a href="make.bhtml">Make a site</a>
      <a href="#get">Get Biggle</a>
    </div>
    <span class="nav-me">
      <biggle-signed-in><span class="dot"></span><biggle-me></biggle-me></biggle-signed-in>
      <biggle-signed-out>Not signed in</biggle-signed-out>
    </span>
  </nav>

  <header class="hero">
    <h1><span class="wordmark" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sr-only">bigglenet</span></h1>
    <p class="tagline">The internet, but smaller and nicer.</p>
    <p class="lede">
      A little web of its own. Sites made by people, at <code>.biggle</code> addresses.
      No ads, no trackers, no cookie banners. The browser simply won't load them.
    </p>
    <div class="fake-bar" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="fake-shield"></span>
      <span class="fake-url"><span id="typed">biggle://home.biggle</span><span class="caret"></span></span>
    </div>
    <p class="hello">
      <biggle-signed-in>Welcome back, <strong><biggle-me></biggle-me></strong>. </biggle-signed-in>
      <biggle-signed-out>You're browsing as a guest. Sign in from the top right to get a Biggle ID. </biggle-signed-out>
      <span id="visits"></span>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="stats" aria-label="The Bigglenet right now">
    <div><strong id="site-count">–</strong><span>sites</span></div>
    <div><strong>0</strong><span>trackers</span></div>
    <div><strong>0</strong><span>ads</span></div>
    <div><strong>1</strong><span>login for everything</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    <article>
      <h2>Ads and trackers can't get in</h2>
      <p>Every page runs in a sealed box. It can't set cookies or load anything from outside the Bigglenet, so there's nothing to track you with.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Everything has a name</h2>
      <p>Sites live at short, memorable addresses like <code>hello.biggle</code>. Type one into the bar and you're there.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>One Biggle ID</h2>
      <p>Make one account and every site can greet you by name. Sites never see your password.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Friends built in</h2>
      <p>Add friends and chat with them right in the browser. Open the people button next to the address bar.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="sites" id="sites">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Sites on the Bigglenet</h2>
      <p>Every <code>.biggle</code> site there is, right now.</p>
    </div>
    <ul id="site-list" class="site-list">
      <li class="loading">Asking the Bigglenet…</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="make">
    <div>
      <h2>Make your own site</h2>
      <p>Pick a name and a look, add some words and pictures, done. The site editor is built into Biggle, and nobody needs to know any code.</p>
      <div class="buttons">
        <a class="button" href="biggle://sites">Make a site</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="make.bhtml">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre class="code"><code><span class="c-head">&lt;!bhtml 1&gt;</span>
&lt;title&gt;My site&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Hello, <span class="c-tag">&lt;biggle-me&gt;</span>guest<span class="c-tag">&lt;/biggle-me&gt;</span>!&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;a href="about.bhtml"&gt;About me&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="get" id="get">
    <h2>Get Biggle</h2>
    <p>You're probably already in it. To take it everywhere:</p>
    <div class="get-grid">
      <a class="get-card" href="https://github.com/bigglenet/bigglenet/releases/latest">
        <strong>Mac, Windows, Linux</strong>
        <span>Download the desktop app. Clicking a <code>biggle://</code> link anywhere opens it.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="get-card" href="https://bigglenet.ethembeldagli.dev">
        <strong>Phone</strong>
        <span>Open the Bigglenet in your phone's browser and add it to your home screen.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="get-card" href="https://github.com/bigglenet/bigglenet">
        <strong>The code</strong>
        <span>Everything is open source. Run your own Bigglenet if you like.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <span class="mark small" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span>home.biggle, made on the Bigglenet.</span>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
